## Technologies

The implementation ports the distinct rendering contracts of all 29 files under Amicro `src/components/mono-charts` plus its 30-row catalog. `GitHubActivity` is an additional variant, not a renamed activity palette. Geometry is pure and data-driven; chart scale/curve/tooltip-position/Sankey helpers are reused. Weighted allocation is calculated from input rather than the upstream demo's fixed CSS grid. A drag captures the pointer on the SVG, so its reading is resolved from coordinates: the pointer is clamped into the union of the mark boxes, `elementFromPoint` finds the mark, and a gap falls to the nearest mark in its column, its row or the plane (`geometry.axis`); the slop, capture, click swallowing and Escape come from the shared `utils/press-scrub.ts`. Request abort/version ownership prevents stale updates, and the shared motion activity helper owns visibility/KeepAlive cleanup. The repository disclosure transition runs only while active and with no reduced-motion preference. No browser API is touched during SVG SSR. Final build, browser and lifecycle verification are performed by the integration owner.
